  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "prop:easyrca-abstention",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "For any finite collection of EasyRCA lag-specific transmission queries on one fixed coordinate set and alphabet family \\(\\mathcal A\\), rank only queries for which the certified partial \\(\\operatorname{TID\\text{-}SCG}\\) returns \\(\\operatorname{SUCCESS}(F)\\).  Under the hypotheses of \\(\\mathrm{thm:cylinder\\text{-}hac}\\), if their population scores are separated by a fixed positive margin, the plug-in ranking is consistent.  A \\(\\operatorname{FAIL}\\) output carries its directly constructed fixed-alphabet lag-switch certificate, and an \\(\\operatorname{UNKNOWN}\\) output records an unresolved query; both are excluded rather than assigned a causal score.",
    "depends_on": [
      "thm:tid-dichotomy",
      "thm:cylinder-hac",
      "prop:finite-margin-plugin-ranking"
    ],
    "justification": "The consumer contract now separates causal scores, certified nonidentification, and unresolved abstention.",
    "gap": "Unknown queries cannot yet be ranked causally.",
    "consumer": "Operators see why each excluded lag is failed or unresolved.",
    "proof_tex": "For every successful query, \\(\\mathrm{thm:tid\\text{-}dichotomy}\\) proves that the returned cylinder functional equals the causal target throughout the compatible class.  Applying \\(\\mathrm{prop:finite\\text{-}margin\\text{-}plugin\\text{-}ranking}\\) to the fixed finite collection of successful functionals shows that, under the stated sampling assumptions and positive population margin, their plug-in ordering is correct with probability tending to one.  The failure branch is sound by the same theorem and carries the explicit lag-switch pair; the unknown branch makes no causal assertion.  Excluding both tags from ranking therefore assigns scores only where a uniform identifying functional has been proved.",
